/*!
    \page qtdbus-security.html
    \title Qt D-Bus Security Considerations
    \ingroup security-considerations
    \brief Security considerations for applications using Qt D-Bus.

    This page covers security considerations for applications using
    \l{Qt D-Bus}.

    \section1 Exporting QObjects directly

    \l{QDBusConnection::registerObject()} can export a \l QObject's own
    slots directly, by passing \l{QDBusConnection::RegisterOption}
    {ExportNonScriptableSlots} or \l{QDBusConnection::RegisterOption}
    {ExportAllSlots}. Doing so makes all of that object's invocables
    accessible remotely, including those inherited from any superclass,
    not only the ones declared on the object's own class. Only
    \l QObject's own built-in slots (such as \l{QObject::deleteLater()}
    {deleteLater()}) are excluded.

    If you need precise, explicit control over which methods are
    bus-callable, use the adaptor pattern instead. See
    \l{Using Qt D-Bus Adaptors} for details.
*/
